<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - May 7.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - May 7.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Feng Kang	 48,000   May 5     May 15     Inchon</p>
<p> Jade Orient     28,000   May 15    May 22     Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   Early June	     Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Delta Trident   35,000   Jun 6		    Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Jade Pacific    28,000   May 3     May 14     KISCO</p>
<p>No vessel calling schedule yet</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Pac Duck	  30,000   May 10    May 27     POSCO</p>
<p> Thornhill	 35,512   May 10		   Kangwon</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Western Friend  36,500   May 10		   POSCO</p>
<p> Aspidoforos     30,500   May 20		   POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p>No vessel calling schedule yet</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
